You **can** file a CFPB complaint against a credit card company — and the process is straightforward.  
Here is the **clear, actionable explanation**, grounded directly in the CFPB’s official guidance.  
All factual statements below are cited from the CFPB and Bankrate sources you saw in the search results.

---

## ⚡ **Short Answer**  
Yes — you can file a complaint with the **Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB)** if a credit card company has engaged in **unfair, deceptive, or abusive practices**, billing errors, refusal to correct mistakes, improper fees, or other violations.  
The CFPB accepts complaints about **credit cards** and forwards them to the company, which must respond — usually within **15 days**.   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/)  [files.consumerfinance.gov](https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_040_2025.pdf)

---

## 🧭 **How to file a CFPB complaint (step‑by‑step)**  
The CFPB outlines a clear process:   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/)  [files.consumerfinance.gov](https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_040_2025.pdf)

### 1. **Go to the CFPB complaint portal**  
**[CFPB Complaint Portal](https://consumerfinance.gov/complaint)**  
(This is the official federal filing system.)

### 2. **Select “Credit cards or prepaid cards”**  
The CFPB explicitly lists **credit cards** as a covered product category.   [files.consumerfinance.gov](https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_040_2025.pdf)

### 3. **Describe the problem clearly**  
Include:  
- key facts in your own words  
- dates  
- amounts  
- communications with the company  
- what resolution you want  
- supporting documents (statements, screenshots, letters)  
The CFPB allows up to **50 pages** of attachments.   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/)

### 4. **Submit the complaint**  
You can file:  
- **Online** (fastest)  
- **By phone**: [855-411-CFPB](tel:8554112372) (180+ languages)   [files.consumerfinance.gov](https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_040_2025.pdf)  
- **By mail**:  
  Consumer Financial Protection Bureau  
  P.O. Box 27170  
  Washington, DC 20038   [files.consumerfinance.gov](https://files.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_040_2025.pdf)

### 5. **CFPB forwards your complaint to the company**  
The CFPB sends your complaint directly to the credit card company and requests a response.  
Most companies respond within **15 days**, and some take up to **60 days** for a final response.   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/process/)

### 6. **You review the company’s response**  
You get **60 days** to provide feedback on whether the company resolved the issue.   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/process/)

---

## 📊 **Why filing a CFPB complaint matters**  
The CFPB uses complaints to:  
- identify systemic problems  
- enforce federal consumer protection laws  
- regulate abusive financial practices  
- publish anonymized complaint data in a public database   [files-prod.consumerfinance.gov](https://files-prod.consumerfinance.gov/f/documents/cfpb_your-money-your-goals_submit-a-complaint_handout_2020-03.pdf)

Your complaint helps **you**, and it also helps **other consumers**.

---

## ⚠️ **Important considerations before filing**  
The CFPB recommends:  
- **Try contacting the credit card company first** — sometimes they fix the issue faster.   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/)  
- If the issue involves **credit reporting errors**, you must dispute with the credit bureau first (required by law).   [Consumer Financial Protection Bureau](https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/)

